#---
# purpose: "a process parked on a receive keeps everything the receive needs across a collection: the pinned list the matcher compares against, the clause body's captured values and the after body; a sender's matching message still wins afterwards"
#---
#
# The parent builds a 2000-element list to pin, prints the size of 20000 more
# cells of garbage so its heap is due for collection, and parks on `^key`. The
# collection that follows the park moves the pinned list, the clause body
# closure that captured `kept` and the after body closure. The child then sends
# an equal list: its probe runs the matcher over the moved pinned list, wins,
# and the parent resumes in the clause body.
def main() do
  parent = self()
  key = Enum.to_list(1..2000)
  kept = [:a, :b, :c]
  dbg(Enum.count(Enum.to_list(1..20000)))
  spawn(fn () -> send(parent, Enum.to_list(1..2000)) end)
  receive do
    ^key -> dbg(kept)
  after
    5000 -> dbg(:timeout)
  end
end
